    "When the dial appears, the rest of the number jumps onto the line in one shot—no stepping between finger cues." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the \"all digits at once\" dial preview.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Your iPhone advertises a **Bluetooth keyboard** (HID). One spectator iPhone pairs once from Settings → Bluetooth, then accepts keystrokes from Carphone CALL during the show.\n\n**Start · Bluetooth** opens the same CallTrick pipeline as Camera (shortcut handoff optional), but the fake dial is a cover: digits you tap on **this** phone also type on the spectator’s Phone app keypad. When the number is recognized, **volume +** (or a hand gesture) drives the rest—first the spectator “frenzy”, then the glitch on your phone, then gesture dialing and the call phase." : {
      "comment" : "A paragraph describing the setup and flow of a single spectator CallTrick.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    }
